%S A144924 1,1,2,4,13,41,196,862,5152,29099,210775,1423622,12186361,96716389,
%T A144924 946272380,8645125518,95760475119,984811345555,12207842942393,
%U A144924 140001673137639,1915231874892898,24256993057067316,363808055968010606,5034204682806843811,82215584740439793662,1235597230083814151052
%N A144924 Number of partition-type permutations in S_n.
%C A144924 These permutations satisfy the condition that their descent set corresponds with a composition which is weakly decreasing under the bijection between subsets of {1,2,...,n-1} to strict compositions of n via {d_1<d_2<...<d_k} maps to (d_1,d_2-d_1,...,d_k-d_k-1,n-d_k)
%C A144924 a(n) / (n!*(2/Pi)^n) tends to 6.9206562992... if n is even, and to 6.519462249... if n is odd. - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 15 2026
%D A144924 R. P. Stanley, Enumerative Combinatorics, Wadsworth, Vol. 1, 1986, Vol. 2, 1999; see especially Chapter 1.
%D A144924 R. P. Stanley, Enumerative Combinatorics, Cambridge, Vol. 2, 1999 (Chapter 7)
%H A144924 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A144924/b144924.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..485</a>
%F A144924 Let F(c_1,...,c_k) be the number of permutations with descent composition (c_1,...,c_k), where n = c_1 + ... + c_k. Then F(n) = 1 and, for k >= 2,
%F A144924 F(c_1,...,c_k) = binomial(n,c_1)*F(c_2,...,c_k) - F(c_1+c_2,c_3,...,c_k).
%F A144924 Thus a(n) = Sum_{lambda partition of n} F(lambda), where the parts of lambda are taken in weakly decreasing order. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Nov 14 2026
%e A144924 For n=3, the 4 partition-type permutations are (1 2 3) (1 3 2) (2 3 1) (3 2 1).
%e A144924 For n = 4, the partitions are (4), (3,1), (2,2), (2,1,1), and (1,1,1,1). Using the recurrence in the Formula section, we first compute:
%e A144924 F(1) = F(2) = F(3) = F(4) = 1,
%e A144924 F(1,1) = binomial(2,1)*F(1) - F(2) = 2 - 1 = 1,
%e A144924 F(2,1) = binomial(3,2)*F(1) - F(3) = 3 - 1 = 2,
%e A144924 F(1,1,1) = binomial(3,1)*F(1,1) - F(2,1) = 3 - 2 = 1.
%e A144924 Then:
%e A144924 F(4) = 1,
%e A144924 F(3,1) = binomial(4,3)*F(1) - F(4) = 4 - 1 = 3,
%e A144924 F(2,2) = binomial(4,2)*F(2) - F(4) = 6 - 1 = 5,
%e A144924 F(2,1,1) = binomial(4,2)*F(1,1) - F(3,1) = 6 - 3 = 3,
%e A144924 F(1,1,1,1) = binomial(4,1)*F(1,1,1) - F(2,1,1) = 4 - 3 = 1.
%e A144924 Hence a(4) = 1 + 3 + 5 + 3 + 1 = 13.
%K A144924 nice,nonn,changed
%O A144924 0,3
